# `t.await(captureContext = true)` — the SAME fast path as the omitted argument. A constant `true` asks for the
# behavior `GetAwaiter()` already has, so it must not pay for the configured awaitable; and since the two are
# behaviorally identical, no runtime assertion can tell them apart (GitHub #64).
+"method":"GetAwaiter"
+System.Runtime.CompilerServices.TaskAwaiter
-"method":"ConfigureAwait"
-ConfiguredTaskAwaitable
